All twenty answers summarise the same sequence of events in the same order:

- the Tangier committee, where Ashley proposes keeping Povy on as Treasurer and Pepys is troubled by it;
- the Navy money report to senior officials, which gets no real answer;
- the merriment at Lady Batten's and supper with his wife and Lady Pen, while he stays vexed.

The differences are only in detail and wording, so they form one group.

Answer 9 is the closest to diverging. It leaves out Ashley's proposal and only says Povy's accounts were discussed and Pepys could not answer an argument. That is vaguer, but it still points to the same event, so it stays in the group.

